No. IC-33646, 2019), since the rule and related staff guidance may have changed by November 2026.\n\nWhat I can say with reasonable confidence: the rule exempts qualifying ETFs from certain Investment Company Act provisions, including the redemption and resale-price provisions of Sections 22(d) and 22(e), subject to conditions. Those conditions generally address:\n\n- **Affiliate limits:** restrictions on affiliated persons acting as authorized participants or otherwise influencing creation and redemption baskets, so that transactions don't favor insiders.\n- **Custom baskets:** written policies and procedures to keep basket construction consistent and non-discriminatory.\n- **Foreign investments:** permission to settle creations and redemptions later than the standard cycle where local market settlement requires it, with conditions on timing.\n\nFor exact conditions, thresholds, and which relief categories apply, consult the rule text or counsel.","ttft_ms":8474,"type":"result","duration_ms":10437,"uuid":"eb2a8741-1a86-4773-a15f-265c247c153c","ttft_stream_ms":403,"time_to_request_ms":54,"first_content_frame_ms":403,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
